{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310665,"nonce":"JbjOaRtxy20dEdkBlqwwPrWK4mg=","title":"2026-09-20 eb68d0ec + 4a7e6e64 (567-\u003e571, TestXML PASS 118): `?x:Int` was typed Int (0 read as null; StringBuf.addSub(s,0,0) copied ...","message":"Closed c5ec8bc, 50c5833. Open from this round: 9ac22e2 (untyped params `S(X, n)` are Dynamic → arithmetic on the box pointer; Sha256/Md5 crash), a0912d8 (blade cache concurrent-write race: test_exception crashes ONLY in a gate right after a parallel conformance run; passes alone — do not chase it as a compiler bug), bd7be74, c3b6c52.\n\n**`?x:Int` → Null\u003cInt\u003e** (`optional_param_type` in decls/fields.rs; applied at lower_parameter, lower_function_param, classes.rs/abstracts.rs pre-computed fn types; NOT ArrowParam). `x:Int = 5` stays Int. Consequences that each needed a fix: (1) callers into IMPORTED callees passed raw scalars into the now-`*u8` slot — `coerce_args_for_cross_module_call` boxes scalar registers bound for Ptr(U8) formals; (2) forward-ref-by-name calls (`Sha1.hex → StringTools.hex(num, 8)`) built the callee signature FROM THE ARGS — `StaticSigIndex::param_kind` now says \"Null\" for `?x:Int` and the site boxes + declares Ptr(U8); (3) `len = b.length - pos` typed Null\u003cInt\u003e but the register is i32 → `maybe_box_value_inner` boxes a scalar REGISTER whenever the target is Optional\u003cscalar\u003e (BytesInput.new faulted); (4) `bind_skipped_optional_args` decided skips by IrType — String vs Ptr(U8) looked bindable → now by Haxe type shape; (5) test_instance_method_default_args expected \"0/value\" for a skipped `?a:Int` — Haxe says \"null/value\"; expectation fixed.\n\n**Null\u003cscalar\u003e operands**: operators.rs unboxed only for Add..Mod. `parsed \u003e= 128` compared the pointer → TRUE. Now Lt/Gt/Le/Ge/Eq/Ne when BOTH sides are scalar-shaped (null literal side keeps the box), plus BitAnd/Or/Xor/Shl/Shr/Ushr. `unbox_optional_args_for_erased_formals` also unboxes for I32/F64/Bool formals of imports (`buf.addChar(c)` with c from parseInt got the pointer).\n\n**target.unicode**: defined (parser/preprocessor.rs default). Parser.hx then calls `buf.addChar(c)` once (the `#if !(target.unicode)` manual UTF-8 path double-encoded because OUR addChar already encodes). But `charCodeAt/unsafeCodeAt` return BYTES, so `StringIteratorUnicode`/`StringKeyValueIteratorUnicode` got an `#elseif rayzor` UTF-8 decode (tolerated per-target branch). Sha256/Md5 take the `Bytes.ofString` path and crash on 9ac22e2, Sha1 fine.\n\n**Array.remove** was `haxe_array_remove(arr, INDEX)`. `Xml.addChild` never detached nodes. Now `haxe_array_remove_value` (bits) via a NEW `map_method!` arm `returns: primitive, raw_value_params` (the old `ptr_params` mask = LEGACY path that boxes an I64 as a truncated Int!), and Array\u003cString\u003e routes through `haxe_array_string_index_of` + `haxe_array_remove_at` in call/array.rs. Mapping row change ⇒ `RAYZOR_WRITE_MAPPING_SNAPSHOT=1 cargo test -p compiler mapping_snapshot`.\n\n**Array literal**: heterogeneity was judged by REGISTER type (String const vs Ptr from a call) → literals boxed, call result raw → `values[0] == \"\u003c\"` faulted. Now by every element's Haxe type (the literal's own type is only its FIRST element's).\n\n**How to apply:** when changing a parameter's representation, grep EVERY place a callee signature is synthesized from call-site ARGS (forward refs, `param_types.push(convert_type(arg.ty))`) — those silently keep the old ABI. `RAYZOR_DUMP_MIR=1` now lists `; extern fnN = @name` so a mystery `call fnN` is resolvable.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_optional_int_params_and_null_scalar_operands` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}